{"step_index":317,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-14T01:07:59Z","input_tokens":2285,"cache_read_tokens":79993,"output_tokens":2012,"thinking":"Remaining targets are 2658. Considering tasks 2 and 3, both of which involve scanning data from two sources, Saramin and Bizno, the design of a combined, high-performance asynchronous scanner script is proposed. This script, tentatively named `deep_scan_stage2.js`, would query both sources for each of the remaining companies. Further analysis is required to determine the optimal approach.\n\n\nThe script will extract phone numbers from both Saramin and Bizno, prioritizing a Korean phone number format validation step for data cleaning. Phone numbers from Saramin will be extracted from JSON-LD or HTML elements, and Bizno's numbers will be extracted from specific table headers, with filters in place to exclude irrelevant entries.  Progress will be saved periodically, and concurrency controls will be implemented to prevent overloading the servers.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"function cleanPhoneNumber(raw) {\\n  if (!raw) return null;\\n  let p = raw.trim();\\n\\n  // Remove HTML tags if any\\n  p = p.replace(/<[^>]+>/g, '').trim();\\n\\n  // Saramin format: +82 051-602-1700 or +82 51-602-1700 or +82 10-1234-5678\\n  p = p.replace(/^\\\\+82\\\\s*/, '');\\n  if (p.startsWith('51-')) p = '0' + p;\\n  if (p.startsWith('2-')) p = '0' + p;\\n  if (p.startsWith('10-')) p = '0' + p;\\n  if (p.startsWith('31-')) p = '0' + p;\\n  if (p.startsWith('70-')) p = '0' + p;\\n\\n  // Clean prefixes like 02-1544, 051-1544, 02-1666, etc.\\n  const prefixMatch = p.match(/^(?:02|051|031)-(1[568][0-9]{2}-[0-9]{4})$/);\\n  if (prefixMatch) p = prefixMatch[1];\\n\\n  // Saramin own CS numbers filter\\n  if (['02-6226-5000', '02-6937-0035', '02-6937-0039', '1577-0000'].includes(p)) {\\n    return null;\\n  }\\n\\n  // Check valid patterns\\n  // 1. Masked 010: 010-xxxx-x***\\n  if (/^01[016789]-[0-9]{3,4}-[0-9*]{4}$/.test(p)) {\\n    return p;\\n  }\\n\\n  // 2. Full phone\\n  const fullRegex = /^(02|03[1-3]|04[1-4]|05[1-5]|06[1-4]|070|01[016789])-[0-9]{3,4}-[0-9]{4}$|^(15[0-9]{2}|16[0-9]{2}|18[0-9]{2})-[0-9]{4}$|^(050[0-9]?)-[0-9]{3,4}-[0-9]{4}$/;\\n  if (fullRegex.test(p)) {\\n    // Avoid bizNo pattern (3-2-5)\\n    if (/^[0-9]{3}-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{5}$/.test(p)) return null;\\n    return p;\\n  }\\n\\n  return null;\\n}\\n\\nconsole.log('+82 051-602-1700 ->', cleanPhoneNumber('+82 051-602-1700'));\\nconsole.log('+82 51-602-1700 ->', cleanPhoneNumber('+82 51-602-1700'));\\nconsole.log('+82 10-5757-9542 ->', cleanPhoneNumber('+82 10-5757-9542'));\\nconsole.log('010-7103-1*** ->', cleanPhoneNumber('010-7103-1***'));\\nconsole.log('02-1544-1234 ->', cleanPhoneNumber('02-1544-1234'));\\nconsole.log('02-6226-5000 ->', cleanPhoneNumber('02-6226-5000'));\\n\"","Description":"\"Verify phone number cleaner logic\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"C:\\\\Users\\\\lg\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\worktrees\\\\resilient-bardeen\\\\find_company_phone_numbers\\\\test_phone_cleaner.js\"","toolAction":"\"Writing test cleaner\"","toolSummary":"\"Test phone number cleaner logic\""}}]}
